.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-oath-access 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-oath\-access \- Manage password protection for OATH
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-oath\-access\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage password protection for OATH
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ckman\-oath\-access\-change(1)
Set or change the OATH password
.TP
ckman\-oath\-access\-remember(1)
Store the device\-bound OATH access key (derived from the password) in the OS keyring to avoid entering the password on each use
.TP
ckman\-oath\-access\-forget(1)
Remove this device\*(Aqs stored access key from the OS keyring
.TP
ckman\-oath\-access\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
